  // 1 to 1.33), leaves the water it has entered: that point's place on the screen. (As Lague's Fluid-Sim does, which
  // has a floor it can find the ray's end on; here the scene is a picture, so it is the picture at that place. It was
  // first the pixel moved along the normal's lean, by a number chosen by eye.)
  let bent = refract(-V, n, 1.0 / 1.33);
